---
import { container, overline, body, focusRing, inlineLink } from "../../utils/designClasses";
import CopyEmailButton from "../CopyEmailButton.astro";
// The Nov 2026 member-driven press release, shown inline on /media as a band
// with progressive disclosure (it replaced the old PressReleaseDialog modal).
// The shareable link is still /media#member-driven-press-release: the section
// carries that id, so the browser scrolls to it, and the script below expands
// the full text. Keep PRESS_RELEASE_ID in sync with the hero link in media.astro.
const PRESS_RELEASE_ID = "member-driven-press-release";

const subhead = "mt-10 text-[22px] font-extrabold leading-snug text-ink min-[810px]:text-[24px]";
const para = "mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-secondary";
---

<section
  id={PRESS_RELEASE_ID}
  aria-labelledby="pr-title"
  class="scroll-mt-6 border-y border-first-light-edge bg-first-light"
>
  <div
    class={`${container} grid gap-x-12 gap-y-6 py-16 min-[810px]:py-20 lg:grid-cols-[12rem_minmax(0,1fr)]`}
  >
    <!-- Meta column: what a journalist checks before reading -->
    <div class="lg:pt-2">
      <p class={overline}>Press release</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base font-bold text-ink">
        <time datetime="2026-11-02">November 2, 2026</time>
      </p>
      <dl class="mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed">
        <dt class="font-bold text-ink">Media contact</dt>
        <dd class="text-ink-secondary">Afzal Mangal</dd>
        <dd class="flex items-center gap-1">
          <a
            id="press-release-contact-email"
            href="mailto:afzal@techforpalestine.org"
            class={`min-w-0 break-all ${inlineLink}`}>afzal@techforpalestine.org</a
          >
          <CopyEmailButton target="press-release-contact-email" />
        </dd>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <article class="min-w-0 max-w-[65ch]">
      <h2
        id="pr-title"
        class="text-[28px] font-extrabold leading-[1.15] text-ink min-[810px]:text-[38px]"
      >
        Tech for Palestine, Behind Apps With More Than 10 Million Users, Becomes a Member-Driven
        Organization
      </h2>

      <p class={`mt-6 text-ink ${body}`}>
        After three years as an incubator, Tech for Palestine is ready for more: more projects,
        built faster, with more impact. That is why it now puts members at the center.
      </p>

      <img
        src="/images/press/t4p-conference-barcelona-2026.webp"
        alt="Tech for Palestine conference in Barcelona, 2026"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
        class="mt-8 aspect-[3/2] h-auto w-full rounded-lg bg-stone object-cover"
      />

      <p class={para}>
        Tech for Palestine (T4P), whose projects have reached more than 10 million users in less
        than three years, today opened its membership to the public. From November 2, anyone can
        become a member and build advocacy projects under the T4P banner. Members get a team to work
        with and the backing of the organization behind Big Tech alternatives such as UpScrolled and
        Thaura, and advocacy tools such as Boycat and NewsCord.
      </p>

      <details data-pr-details class="group mt-8">
        <summary
          class={`inline-flex min-h-[44px] cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-2 rounded-pill border border-ink px-5 py-3 text-[13px] font-bold text-ink transition-colors hover:border-grove hover:text-grove motion-reduce:transition-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden ${focusRing}`}
        >
          <span class="group-open:hidden">Read the full release</span>
          <span class="hidden group-open:inline">Hide the full release</span>
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke="currentColor"
            class="h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 motion-reduce:transition-none"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"
            ></path>
          </svg>
        </summary>

        <div class="pt-4">
          <h3 class={subhead}>From incubator to member-driven organization</h3>
          <p class={para}>
            For the past three years, the T4P incubator helped the people behind more than 90
            initiatives turn their ideas into advocacy tools. Those teams received mentorship,
            connections and support, but the building itself happened in their own organizations,
            outside T4P.
          </p>
          <p class={para}>
            T4P is now bringing the building inside. The support it offered external teams is
            available to every member. New projects carry the T4P name, and members build them
            together.
          </p>
          <blockquote class="my-10">
            <p class="text-[22px] font-extrabold leading-snug text-ink min-[810px]:text-[26px]">
              <span class="text-grove" aria-hidden="true">“</span>Our incubator proved that small
              teams with the right skills can build tools used by millions. Now we build with many
              more people, and with far less distance between an idea and the team that ships it.<span
                class="text-grove"
                aria-hidden="true">”</span
              >
            </p>
          </blockquote>

          <h3 class={subhead}>How membership works</h3>
          <p class={para}>
            Members join with the skills they have: engineering, design, research, writing or
            organizing. Some join an existing project that needs their expertise. Others bring their
            own idea and start a new team, which T4P mentors help scope, staff with fellow members
            and take to a first public version.
          </p>
          <p class={para}>
            The model can move fast. When Macklemore was dropped from Ed Sheeran’s US tour after
            saying “Free Palestine” on stage, he explained that Sheeran could not get past his
            public stance of “I don’t take sides.” T4P members picked up the moment and built Ed
            Takes No Sides, a directory where artists who do take a stand for Palestine can create a
            profile and be found.
          </p>

          <h3 class={subhead}>25+ projects from a 200-member private beta</h3>
          <p class={para}>
            Before the public launch, T4P tested membership for several months with 200 members. In
            that time, members built more than 25 new advocacy projects, including:
          </p>
          <ul
            class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-secondary marker:text-grove"
          >
            <li>Israel Bonds Tracker, a platform that raises awareness about Israeli bonds.</li>
            <li>
              Sponsored internships connecting students from Gaza with internships in the UK and
              Ireland.
            </li>
            <li>
              Profile Pic Maker, revived by members: a tool that adds a Palestinian-flag frame to
              social media profile pictures.
            </li>
            <li>
              A research team investigating bias against Palestinians in frontier large language
              models.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class={subhead}>Two ways to join</h3>
          <p class={para}>
            <strong class="font-bold text-ink">Members</strong> contribute time and skills. They can
            join an existing team or form a new one with members who complement their skills. Sign-up
            is at <a href="/membership" class={inlineLink}>techforpalestine.org/membership</a>, and
            the T4P team helps each new member find a first project.
          </p>
          <p class={para}>
            <strong class="font-bold text-ink">Supporting members</strong> back the work financially
            and leave the building to others. Their dues fund the marketing, engineering, mentorship,
            software access, partnerships and grants that T4P provides to its projects. Details are at
            <a href="/supporting-member" class={inlineLink}
              >techforpalestine.org/supporting-member</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  // Expand the full release when someone arrives on (or navigates to) the
  // shareable #member-driven-press-release link, and keep the analytics event
  // the old dialog fired so the "Press Release Opened" goal stays continuous.
  const ID = "member-driven-press-release";
  const HASH = `#${ID}`;
  const details = document.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>(`#${ID} [data-pr-details]`);

  if (details) {
    details.addEventListener("toggle", () => {
      if (details.open) window.plausible?.("Press Release Opened", { props: { id: ID } });
    });

    const openFromHash = () => {
      if (location.hash === HASH) details.open = true;
    };
    openFromHash();
    window.addEventListener("hashchange", openFromHash);
  }
</script>
